+**3.18 Leave no FM sub-audio on in DMR.** Symptom: after a channel change or a scan that passed an FM channel with a
+receive CTCSS or DCS tone, every DMR, NXDN, P25 and YSF over keyed and counted as sent but nobody decoded it, until a
+restart; on the power-on channel it worked. Cause: the FD6818's sub-audio register 0x51 kept the FM channel's receive
+tone, and its bit 15 also turns on the chip's sub-audio transmitter, so the tone rode on the 4FSK. Rule: the RF chip
+driver turns the sub-audio off when it enters DMR (`fd6818_set_mode`; `fd6818sh_dmr_mode` already does), not each
+board's tune path. Radios: boards with the FD6818 as the transceiver. Test: `test_dmr_tone_off` (fd6818Test).
+
